### 5. `@session-start-activity-timeline` Spec — Full Content

**File:** `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/modules/cli.yaml`, line 5599

**Slug:** `session-start-activity-timeline`  
**ULID:** `01KJ74T85REJ1B436WE944N061`  
**Status:** `implementation: in_progress`, `maturity: draft`

**Description:** Merge recently completed tasks and git commits into a single chronological "Recent Activity" timeline. Commits matched to tasks via `Task: @slug` trailer in commit body. Deduplicates linked entries. Replaces separate "Recently Completed" and "Recent Commits" sections in human output. Raw arrays preserved in JSON.

**Acceptance Criteria:**

| AC ID | Given | When | Then |
|---|---|---|---|
| `ac-activity-merge` | completed tasks and git commits exist | recent activity section renders | both sources appear in a single chronological list |
| `ac-activity-trailer-link` | a commit has `Task: @slug` trailer in its body | recent activity renders | that commit shows linked task info alongside it |
| `ac-activity-sort` | activity items have mixed timestamps | timeline renders | task groups sorted by most recent event (completion or latest commit); commits within a group sorted chronologically |
| `ac-activity-dedup` | multiple commits are linked to the same task via `Task: @slug` trailers | timeline renders | commits are grouped under a single task entry as nested children, not shown as separate top-level entries |
| `ac-activity-no-git` | `--no-git` flag is passed | activity timeline renders | only task completions shown, no commit entries |
| `ac-activity-hierarchy` | linked commits and completed tasks exist | human-readable timeline renders | tasks are top-level entries and linked commits appear nested beneath their task with a visual connector |
| `ac-activity-orphan` | a commit has no `Task: @slug` trailer | human-readable timeline renders | the commit appears as a standalone indented entry visually distinct from task entries |

**Traits attached:** none (the `traits: []` field is empty)

**Depends on:** `@session-start-unlocks`

---

### Key Gap: What Is NOT Yet Implemented

The current implementation satisfies `ac-activity-merge`, `ac-activity-trailer-link`, `ac-activity-sort`, `ac-activity-no-git`, and the basic `ac-activity-dedup` (only one `linked_commit` entry per commit). However:

- **`ac-activity-hierarchy`** — Tasks should be top-level entries with linked commits nested beneath using a visual connector. Currently all items render flat at the same indent.
- **`ac-activity-dedup` (multi-commit grouping)** — The spec says "multiple commits grouped under a single task entry as nested children." The data model only produces ONE `linked_commit` per commit (uses `break` after first match), so if multiple commits reference the same task, each becomes its own `linked_commit` entry rather than being grouped.
- **`ac-activity-orphan`** — Orphan commits should be "visually distinct" from linked commits. Currently they look identical in format; there's no indent or prefix distinction.

The in-progress task (`@task-hierarchical-activity-timeline`, ULID `01KJ91Q8BVDS75TV60KVRX5EKC`) was opened specifically to implement the hierarchical display — grouping commits under their task with a visual connector (pipe/bent arrow), and making orphan commits visually distinct. The task note confirms: "primarily a display-layer change to the session start human formatter. The activity_timeline data already has `linked_commit` type with task refs, so grouping logic can work from the existing data structure."

